<title>BELGIUM: Coceral changes 1997 EU winter barley area.</title>
<headline>Coceral changes 1997 EU winter barley area.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coceral, the EU grain trade lobby, corrected upwards on Friday the EU 1997 winter barley area to 5.42 million hectares, from 4.78 million ha.</p>
<p>It also amended the total EU winter grain area to 24.77 million ha, from 24.12 million ha.</p>
<p>Coceral said it had corrected the year and the surface sown with winter barley in Germany to 1.47 million ha in 1997/98 and 1.41 million ha in 1996/97, from 827,000 tonnes and 795,000 tonnes respectively.</p>
<p>The forecast winter area for each cereal was (million ha):</p>
<p>				  1997	    1996    pct change</p>
<p> Total Winter Area	  24.766	  24.145    +2.6</p>
<p>Of which:  Soft wheat		   13.971	  13.352    +2.9</p>
<p> Durum wheat		   2.995	   2.943    +1.8</p>
<p> Barley			  5.419	   5.332    +1.6</p>
<p> Rye			     1.166	   1.187    -1.7</p>
<p> Oats			    0.425	   0.423    +0.5</p>
<p> Triticale		     0.790	   0.688   +14.8</p>
</text>
